# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live settings file holds the credential encryption key and the JWT signing key. Anyone who
# can read them can decrypt every stored camera password and forge a session as any user, so the
# file stays local. config/trinetra.settings.example.json is the committed template — copy it and
# fill in your own values:
#
#     cp config/trinetra.settings.example.json config/trinetra.settings.json
#
config/trinetra.settings.json

# Environment files for systemd hosts. deploy/systemd/*.env.example are the committed templates.
*.env
!*.env.example

# Key material of any kind.
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore

# Local database dumps: a dump of a real deployment contains sealed credentials and event data.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.backup

# Logs and process files from local runs.
*.log
*.pid
